\details{
Every \code{receive} player must be on another team's roster: the team that
rosters them is the trade partner, and is scored with the same swap in
reverse. If \code{receive} players come from more than one team, the partner
side can't be split up and only \code{teamId} is scored, with a warning. A free
agent or player on waivers is an error -- that's a pickup, not a trade.

Passing more than one \code{scoringPeriodId} scores the same swap at each week
separately (rosters, byes, and matchups all change week to week). Use
\code{scoringPeriodId = "rest"} to score every week from the current one through
the end of the regular season. That makes one API request per week, so it
takes a few seconds; sum \code{delta} by \code{teamId} for a rest-of-season total.

If a team ends up with more players than the league's roster limit (not
counting players on IR), its lowest-scoring non-starters are listed in
\code{dropped}. Dropping non-starters never changes the starting score, so this
says who you'd have to cut rather than changing the result. A warning is
given if the league's trade deadline has passed.
